# The image is FROM scratch and performs exactly one COPY, so nothing here can
# leak into it — this file only keeps the build context small.
#
# Exclusions are LISTED rather than written as `*` plus `!build` re-includes.
# The negation form is what broke the first CI run: this file still said
# `!dist/envpilot` after the Dockerfile moved to build/<os>/<arch>/, so `*`
# excluded everything, the context transferred 2 bytes, and the COPY failed
# with an opaque "failed to compute cache key ... not found". An explicit list
# fails toward sending too much, which is slow, instead of too little, which
# is a broken build.
node_modules
src
scripts
*.md
*.json
*.ts
LICENSE
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.gitignore
.turbo
*.mjs
